        "turn_tail": "rst check |\n\nThe other two allowed paths (`autoreiv_concurrent_job_b.md`, `autoreiv_kill_resume_mid_job.md`) are tangential (concurrency, kill/resume) and not needed for a standing-Job summary.\n\n---\n\n### Execution plan (Phase 2)\n\n| # | Action | Tool | Risk / HITL |\n|---|--------|------|-------------|\n| 1 | **Create** the note in `00_Inbox/` \u2014 \u2264 120-word body, all facts sourced from the three notes above, cross-linked | `wiki_note_create` | high / **HITL** |\n| 2 | **Read** it back to confirm it exists and opens \u2192 satisfies done-when | `wiki_note_read` | low / no |\n\n### Draft body (~108 words)\n\n> A **standing Job** in AutoReiv loops rather than terminates. Each cycle it re-checks its done-when and re-queues itself, unlike a one-shot Job that hits Done/Failed and stops.\n>\n> **Phases:** Formulate \u2192 Execute, repeated every cycle.\n>\n> **Still minted:** the same 5-field contract (goal, facts, constraints, done-when, budget) is stamped at creation. Budget is per-cycle, with an optional lifetime cap.\n>\n> **HITL gate:** high-risk tools like `wiki_note_create` park the job for explicit human approval before content lands.\n>\n> **Can end:** explicit cancel, lifetime budget exhausted, or a done-when that finally holds.\n>\n> In one sentence: a standing Job is a loop with a gate.\n\n**Sources:** `standing_job_in_autoreiv.md` \u00b7 `standing_jobs_priming_schema.md` \u00b7 `card_236_job_mint_in_autoreiv.md`\n\n---\n\n**Ready to execute** on your go-ahead (step 1 requires HITL approval for `wiki_note_create`).",
